    {
      "id": "1f8d166d-31f8-4fe5-ab68-208191e1c47e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -992,
        -672
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Automated Watch Service Shop CRM sync & AI Quotation\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow captures a watch service request from a form, normalizes customer details, and syncs the contact with GoHighLevel. It restores and analyzes the uploaded watch photo, checks image authenticity, then uses a Gemini-powered AI agent to generate a structured repair quotation. The final ticket is logged to Google Sheets and routed either to manual review notifications or automated customer/shop emails.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the form trigger with the expected customer, email, watch details, and photo upload fields.\n- Connect GoHighLevel credentials and confirm the lookup/upsert fields match your CRM contact schema.\n- Add Sightengine API credentials or request parameters for image authenticity detection.\n- Configure the Google Gemini chat model credentials and verify the structured output parser schema matches the ticket/quotation fields expected downstream.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the target spreadsheet/tab with columns for ticket ID, customer details, estimate, review status, and timestamps.\n- Connect Gmail credentials and update sender/recipient addresses for customer estimates, shop notifications, and manual review alerts.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the manual review threshold, AI quotation prompt/pricing logic, Google Sheet columns, and email templates to match the shop\u2019s service categories and approval process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "16cf68cf-acf9-42ae-b156-7a95945f179e",
